  VERDICT: the sphere idea is real physics — every mass already IS an activated sphere: it pulls in the
  medium (M_c = 5.364 M_b within 5.84 r_M) and carries a locked-amplitude field g_ph = sqrt(G M_b a0)/r.
  But the framework's own constants close the device version: (1) stiffness screens lab scales by
  (d/L*)^2 ~ 1e-34 (the medium only responds at L* >= 5.75 pc scales); (2) the amplitude is locked —
  1 g at 1 m needs a 1.5e22 kg planetoid, no activation multiplies it; (3) no coupling exists to
  'activate' the medium (E6; every portal closed); (4) the medium's dynamics are glacial (4.3 yr).
  The sphere works — at galactic scales, where it is called a galaxy: the settled halo IS the medium
  pulled in, and ARGON02's ESD is its measurable signature.
